  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 Number of new data sources used at Country Office level.
1.2 Diversity of different data sources used.
1.3 Number of sustainable development solutions identified and documented  
1.4 Number of innovation methods used to test and iterate over the different hypotheses.
2.1 Number of publications and communication stories the Accelerator Lab Network shares with a public audience (outside of UNDP)
2.2 Number of UNDP Country Office programming influenced by the Accelerator Lab Network&#x2019;s work and methodologies
3.1 Number of network interactions among the Accelerator Labs
3.2 Number  of new models, approaches, and insights documented and disseminated throughout the network.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">0 for all indicators</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Waste Experiment in Batumi and Samtredia
2. Solution Safari
3. Horizon scaning (identify 6 main problems)
4. weak signals in energy sector (Conducting research)
5. Ukraine + RU/BE refugees in Georgia (Conducting research)
6. Data Visualization (Delieverables in Abkhazia)
7. FutureAgroChallange ( analyses and reccomendations)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Done - Experiment was conducted 
2. Done - Solution Safari was conducted
3. Partially done (identified 4 problems out of 6)
4. Partially done (research is on going)
5. Done - Research conducted
6. Done - Info graph was published
7. Done - Report was delivered</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 - 2 new sources of data per year
1.2 - 1 different type of data sources per year 
1.3 - at least 15 sustainable solutions identified
1.4 - at least 2 innovative methods used to test or iterate hypotheses. 
2.1 - at least 5 blogs published and at least 5 tv/radio/podcast visits 
2.2 - at least 3 projects at CO office level influenced/engaged by the Lab. 
3.1 - At least 5 other labs engaged for experience exchange and collaboration opportunities.
3.2 - at least 1 new method, model or approach documented and disseminated</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 - Using GeoStat and NCDC data was calculated approximate date of reaching 60-70 percent vaccination of the Georgian population.
1.2 - AccLab partnered with Forset to develop and implement a single data-based communication campaign in social media. AccLab developed 18 info-products and reached more than 1200 000 online users during 6 months of the campaign. 
1.3 - In 2021 AccLab supported 2 hackathons, 1 ideathon, and 1 idea challenge as a way to find new innovative solutions to Georgia&#x2019;s challenges. As a result, one bio-packaging startup was established, and 5 applications/web platform prototypes were developed and more than 60 solutions identified. 
1.4 - The UNDP Accelerator Lab organized a workshop during the Future Agro Challenge event aiming to identify the innovators in the agricultural field. During the workshop, innovative methods such as design thinking and sense making were used to map the barriers faced by the agro innovators and agro-tech startups
AccLab is implementing a Behavioral experiment to support plastic waste separation at source in two Georgian cities - Tbilisi and Batumi. Together with Tbilisi and Batumi City Halls, and in consultation with Packaging Cluster Project, AccLab is implementing PET waste separation experiment, which involves cooperation between local NGOs, municipal services, volunteers, and a private entity (waste recycling company).
2.1 - Accelerator Lab published 5 Blogs and participated up to 10 TV/radio/podcast shows.
3.1 - AccLab has been sharing its tools and expertise with 5 other labs on behavioral insights, data communication, and online solutions safari. These are AccLabs from North Macedonia, Ukraine, Syria, Saudi Arabia and Panama.
3.2 - AccLab Georgia has documented the waste experiment conducted using the behavioral science. The knowledge product includes lessons learned, tips and advices for the similar experiments.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. The accelerator lab of Georgia staff is recruited.
2. The accelerator lab staff is trained at the AccLab Bootcamp training.
3. Explored the current CO portfolio.
4. Potential frontier challenges to be explored and identified.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UNDP accelerator lab in Georgia was established at the end of 2020. This did not allow much time for the lab to work towards the targets set for year 1. Based on the 100 days Action Plan and activities the Lab completed the followings can be outlined: 
1. All 3 Heads are recruited in October-November 2020.
2. The lab staff is participated in dedicated 6-week training during the AccLab Bootcamp in November-December 2020. 
3. The lab conducted meetings with RR, DRR and CO teams and studied existing UNDP portfolio and priorities.
4. Based on conducted meetings with RR, DRR and CO clusters, the lab identified the 3 most important challenges and developed 100-day action plan.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
